WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.255
[MUSIC]

00:00:02.255 --> 00:00:04.767
To an entrepreneur and investor is

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:07.192
somebody that you confide in when

00:00:07.192 --> 00:00:09.011
you have difficulties,

00:00:09.011 --> 00:00:10.916
somebody that you can have

00:00:10.916 --> 00:00:13.429
meaningful conversations with,

00:00:13.429 --> 00:00:15.162
who can challenge you,

00:00:15.162 --> 00:00:17.261
who can be a sounding board.

00:00:17.261 --> 00:00:19.886
Somebody who can open up doors,

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:22.712
Reaction represents all of that.

00:00:22.712 --> 00:00:26.495
[MUSIC]

00:00:26.495 --> 00:00:28.225
&gt;&gt; So Reaction was launched on

00:00:28.225 --> 00:00:29.806
campus from the Stanford

00:00:29.806 --> 00:00:31.168
executive program.

00:00:31.168 --> 00:00:33.484
&gt;&gt; This idea of how do you bring

00:00:33.484 --> 00:00:36.004
a community together that can

00:00:36.004 --> 00:00:39.341
elevate entrepreneurs experiences.

00:00:39.341 --> 00:00:40.771
&gt;&gt; We had 225 leaders from

00:00:40.771 --> 00:00:42.072
throughout the world,

00:00:42.072 --> 00:00:43.958
every continent, we set a mission

00:00:43.958 --> 00:00:45.648
to improve a billion lives this

00:00:45.648 --> 00:00:47.599
decade by scaling innovations that

00:00:47.599 --> 00:00:48.980
would change the world.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:51.693
&gt;&gt; I was all in.

00:00:51.693 --> 00:00:54.035
&gt;&gt; We have alumni from the Stanford

00:00:54.035 --> 00:00:56.292
executive program classes all

00:00:56.292 --> 00:00:58.555
the way from 2014 to 22.

00:00:58.555 --> 00:00:59.927
&gt;&gt; We really enjoyed being

00:00:59.927 --> 00:01:00.675
together.

00:01:00.675 --> 00:01:02.099
So the first thing we thought

00:01:02.099 --> 00:01:03.342
about is, hey, how do we

00:01:03.342 --> 00:01:05.285
keep this community going together?

00:01:05.285 --> 00:01:06.420
&gt;&gt; We had three problems we were

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:07.792
trying to solve, the first was how

00:01:07.792 --> 00:01:08.940
could we continue to learn?

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.597
&gt;&gt; I believe in lifelong learning.

00:01:10.597 --> 00:01:12.444
The way you consume information,

00:01:12.444 --> 00:01:14.035
the way you learn these days,

00:01:14.035 --> 00:01:15.508
that has changed forever.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:17.099
&gt;&gt; The second was thinking about

00:01:17.099 --> 00:01:18.247
what we could build.

00:01:18.247 --> 00:01:20.086
&gt;&gt; We were a group of 225,

00:01:20.086 --> 00:01:22.262
you realized the potential and

00:01:22.262 --> 00:01:23.105
the power.

00:01:23.105 --> 00:01:24.635
&gt;&gt; And then the third was around

00:01:24.635 --> 00:01:26.039
purpose, thinking about

00:01:26.039 --> 00:01:27.696
what we'd want to look back on,

00:01:27.696 --> 00:01:29.416
what will we be proud about, and

00:01:29.416 --> 00:01:30.947
to collectively accomplish

00:01:30.947 --> 00:01:32.286
something that none of us

00:01:32.286 --> 00:01:34.287
ever could have done individually.

00:01:36.409 --> 00:01:38.137
So in terms of improving a billion

00:01:38.137 --> 00:01:39.124
lives, we focus on

00:01:39.124 --> 00:01:40.976
the macro-problems of the world in

00:01:40.976 --> 00:01:42.829
health of course, heart disease,

00:01:42.829 --> 00:01:44.683
mental health, chronic disease,

00:01:44.683 --> 00:01:46.740
and most recently, sustainability.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:50.709
&gt;&gt; I became involved with Reaction

00:01:50.709 --> 00:01:52.833
because I am a founder of a local

00:01:52.833 --> 00:01:54.961
bio manufacturing company and

00:01:54.961 --> 00:01:57.190
we were looking for investors.

00:01:57.190 --> 00:01:59.322
What Mango Materials is focused on

00:01:59.322 --> 00:02:01.453
is changing the plastics industry

00:02:01.453 --> 00:02:02.990
completely.

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:04.358
So we're looking for

00:02:04.358 --> 00:02:06.562
a very specific type of investor,

00:02:06.562 --> 00:02:08.690
one who sees the future in the same

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:09.384
way we do.

00:02:09.384 --> 00:02:10.824
We are technologists,

00:02:10.824 --> 00:02:12.984
we are engineers and scientists who

00:02:12.984 --> 00:02:15.144
have created this new technology,

00:02:15.144 --> 00:02:17.232
but we need partners and investors

00:02:17.232 --> 00:02:18.969
to help us see this through.

00:02:18.969 --> 00:02:21.063
&gt;&gt; Innovator like Molly has a lot

00:02:21.063 --> 00:02:23.324
of support in terms of capital,

00:02:23.324 --> 00:02:25.248
what we need to do is to bring

00:02:25.248 --> 00:02:27.176
something to Molly that's

00:02:27.176 --> 00:02:28.114
different.

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:29.688
&gt;&gt; So Reaction helps by

00:02:29.688 --> 00:02:31.909
facilitating the scaling of

00:02:31.909 --> 00:02:34.042
the technology globally.

00:02:34.042 --> 00:02:35.825
&gt;&gt; By organizing a global set of

00:02:35.825 --> 00:02:37.905
Stanford alumni into this fund,

00:02:37.905 --> 00:02:39.761
we're able to help her to open

00:02:39.761 --> 00:02:41.917
doors throughout the world in a way

00:02:41.917 --> 00:02:43.849
that is creating more value and

00:02:43.849 --> 00:02:45.807
improving more lives faster.

00:02:45.807 --> 00:02:47.690
&gt;&gt; We see climate change and

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:49.843
plastic pollution has two of

00:02:49.843 --> 00:02:51.996
the largest threats that our

00:02:51.996 --> 00:02:53.891
planet is facing today.

00:02:53.891 --> 00:02:55.402
In order for these solutions,

00:02:55.402 --> 00:02:56.449
these innovations,

00:02:56.449 --> 00:02:58.134
the science to reach the different

00:02:58.134 --> 00:02:59.819
parts of the planet it can impact,

00:02:59.819 --> 00:03:01.504
it needs to have the leadership and

00:03:01.504 --> 00:03:02.899
influence in those areas and

00:03:02.899 --> 00:03:03.963
we can provide that.

00:03:03.963 --> 00:03:06.031
&gt;&gt; So by being part of an ecosystem

00:03:06.031 --> 00:03:08.337
of changemakers, who believe the

00:03:08.337 --> 00:03:10.644
world can be changed through novel

00:03:10.644 --> 00:03:13.109
innovation and new technologies and

00:03:13.109 --> 00:03:14.858
new business platforms,

00:03:14.858 --> 00:03:17.004
that gives us a path to the future

00:03:17.004 --> 00:03:19.012
that we all really want to see.

00:03:19.012 --> 00:03:20.462
&gt;&gt; And in terms of the industries

00:03:20.462 --> 00:03:22.086
that are impacted between energy

00:03:22.086 --> 00:03:23.768
and health and transportation and

00:03:23.768 --> 00:03:25.450
manufacturing and agriculture,

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:26.552
we have access to all of

00:03:26.552 --> 00:03:28.068
these different industries.

00:03:28.068 --> 00:03:29.472
And play a unique role in helping

00:03:29.472 --> 00:03:30.252
them to plug in and

00:03:30.252 --> 00:03:31.656
to connect with the leaders that

00:03:31.656 --> 00:03:32.852
can influence decisions,

00:03:32.852 --> 00:03:34.048
collectively we can help to

00:03:34.048 --> 00:03:35.715
solve the climate crisis challenge.

00:03:39.621 --> 00:03:40.691
On campus at the GSB,

00:03:40.691 --> 00:03:42.355
we focused a lot on their slogan,

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:43.663
which is to change lives,

00:03:43.663 --> 00:03:45.090
change organizations, and

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:46.880
change the world.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:48.115
Naturally, as leaders come

00:03:48.115 --> 00:03:48.733
to Stanford,

00:03:48.733 --> 00:03:50.276
their lives are transformed, they

00:03:50.276 --> 00:03:52.390
can transform their organizations.

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:53.428
But changing the world,

00:03:53.428 --> 00:03:54.616
we thought we can really play

00:03:54.616 --> 00:03:55.464
an important role.

00:03:55.464 --> 00:03:56.940
&gt;&gt; Changing the world,

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:59.236
the best thing you can do is enable

00:03:59.236 --> 00:04:01.779
entrepreneurs to build companies,

00:04:01.779 --> 00:04:03.419
enable them to invest in

00:04:03.419 --> 00:04:05.808
communities with global impact.

00:04:05.808 --> 00:04:07.862
&gt;&gt; Makes Reaction different is our

00:04:07.862 --> 00:04:09.536
community of investors,

00:04:09.536 --> 00:04:11.742
of executives, of entrepreneurs

00:04:11.742 --> 00:04:13.491
throughout the world, and

00:04:13.491 --> 00:04:15.315
their desire to be hands on to

00:04:15.315 --> 00:04:17.140
be active in terms of helping

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:19.421
the innovators to really take their

00:04:19.421 --> 00:04:21.627
solutions further than they could

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:22.713
go on their own.

00:04:22.713 --> 00:04:24.578
So our ambition is to create

00:04:24.578 --> 00:04:27.173
the most global, most influential,

00:04:27.173 --> 00:04:29.120
and most impactful Stanford

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:32.070
investment community in the world.

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:33.812
We're very proud of what's been

00:04:33.812 --> 00:04:35.303
accomplished so far, but so

00:04:35.303 --> 00:04:37.044
excited for where this is going to

00:04:37.044 --> 00:04:38.410
go in the future and seeing

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:40.107
this dream really come to life.

00:04:40.107 --> 00:04:41.726
I'm Molly Morse, CEO and

00:04:41.726 --> 00:04:43.865
co-founder of Mango Materials.

00:04:43.865 --> 00:04:45.423
&gt;&gt; My name is Babu Sivadasan,

00:04:45.423 --> 00:04:47.050
one of the founding partners

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:47.876
of Reaction.

00:04:47.876 --> 00:04:49.100
I'm Dan Matthies,

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.469
I'm a co-founder and

00:04:50.469 --> 00:04:52.419
managing partner of Reaction.

